cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LongevityOS data or code, please cite it as below."
title: "LongevityOS: an evidence atlas of longevity-drug candidates and a volunteer screening swarm"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PhotonBounce"
  - name: "LongevityOS contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PhotonBounce/longevityos"
url: "https://photon-bounce.com/longevityos/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - longevity
  - geroscience
  - virtual screening
  - volunteer computing
  - evidence atlas
abstract: >-
  LongevityOS is an open evidence atlas of compounds studied for lifespan and
  healthspan (including every rigorous null), a human-evidence ledger of
  interventions with all-cause-mortality data, and a browser-based volunteer
  compute swarm that screens harvested molecules against known longevity-active
  reference compounds with a deterministic, two-party-verified pipeline. The
  screening output is a ranked shortlist of hypotheses, never a discovery or a
  recommendation. Data is CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA); code is MIT.
